        bio: "José “Joe” Silva, 55, skipper of the dragger SANTA MARIA, which lands at Pier 3 with the Castellano boats. His older brother António came first, went to France with the Yankee Division and was killed in the Argonne in October 1918; Joe came over from São Miguel the next year, “to take his place,” his mother said. Carries the statue at the Blessing of the Fleet every June. Mends nets on Saturday mornings, and lets his knees complain.",
